--- CRITERION 2: readTransferDecision reads the FILE, not in-memory echo --- MET
resolve_test.go:56-68. Three independent lines of evidence:
(a) Fresh instance, not the writer's: `peek := dataloader.New(dir, deps.Store)`
    (resolve_test.go:58). dataloader.New (loader.go:176-183) constructs a new DataLoader
    with empty maps; the loader that performed the write is deps.Transfers, a DIFFERENT
    instance created in newDeps (register_test.go:31-36). No decision state is carried over.
(b) The read path terminates at os.ReadFile: LoadTransferDecisions
    (dataloader/transfer_decisions.go:34-38) -> loadTransferDecisionsLocked:41 ->
    tx.ReadFile(dl.transferDecisionsPath()) (storage.go:720-726 -> Storage.ReadFileContext
    :226). Storage does keep a byte cache, but encodeForWrite `delete(s.cache, path)`
    (storage.go:327-330) invalidates the entry on every write, and the cache is additionally
    validated on os.Stat modTime+size (storage.go:232-247). So after the tool's write the
    read is a real os.ReadFile of <tmpdir>/transfer_decisions.json, JSON-unmarshalled
    (transfer_decisions.go:53-59).
(c) EMPIRICAL and decisive: under the criterion-3 mutation the helper returned "reject"
    while the test's input argument and out.Verdict were "confirm". It cannot be echoing
    the input. Also, `t.Fatalf("no persisted decision for pair_key %q ...")` (resolve_test.go
    :64-66) means a no-write mutation fails too, not silently passes.

